From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: keep WED running if WO rx stats can't be
 enabled

mt7915_dma_start() returned early when the WO rx statistics command
failed, skipping mtk_wed_device_start() and the interrupt setup, and its
callers ignore the error, so WED stayed stopped after a recovery. The
rx statistics only feed station counters: warn and carry on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/dma.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/dma.c b/mt7915/dma.c
index dd39fbad..4564245d 100644
--- a/mt7915/dma.c
+++ b/mt7915/dma.c
@@ -316,9 +316,13 @@ int mt7915_dma_start(struct mt7915_dev *dev, bool reset, bool wed_reset)
 		else
 			mt76_wr(dev, MT_INT_MASK_CSR, wed_irq_mask);
 
+		/* WO rx counters only feed station statistics, don't leave
+		 * WED and the interrupts disabled if they can't be enabled
+		 */
 		ret = mt7915_mcu_wed_enable_rx_stats(dev);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			dev_warn(mdev->dev,
+				 "failed to enable WED rx stats: %d\n", ret);
 
 		mtk_wed_device_start(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed, wed_irq_mask);
 	}
